.TH MUFFLE 1 "November 2026" "Muffle 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
muffle \- suppress successful command output and show useful failure details
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B muffle
.RI [ options ] " -- command " [ arguments ... ]
.br
.B muffle --help | --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Muffle runs a command directly, captures its standard output and standard
error into one log, and suppresses captured output when the command succeeds.
On failure it prints a bounded tail and the log path. It returns the child
status, mapping signal termination to 128 plus the signal number.
.PP
Muffle does not parse a shell command string. Shell syntax requires an
explicit shell command, for example
.BR "muffle -- sh -c 'make && make test'" .
The POSIX execvp API may use /bin/sh for an executable text file rejected
with ENOEXEC; this is executable-format fallback, not parsing of arguments.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Print usage information and exit successfully.
.TP
.B --version
Print the compiled version and exit successfully.
.TP
.BI "--tail " N
Display at most the final N output lines on failure. N must be a positive
integer. The default is 40.
.TP
.B --verbose
Stream captured output to Muffle's standard output while retaining it in the
log.
.TP
.BI "--log " PATH
Create a persistent log at PATH. The path must not already exist. Muffle
requests file mode 0600.
.TP
.B --
End Muffle option parsing. The following arguments form the child command.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Child succeeded, or help/version was printed.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line arguments.
.TP
.B 125
Muffle internal failure.
.TP
.B 126
The command was found but could not be executed.
.TP
.B 127
The command could not be found.
.TP
.B other values
The normal child exit code, or 128 plus the signal number if signal-killed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TMPDIR
Directory used for temporary logs. Defaults to /tmp when unset.
The child inherits the invoking environment.
.SH FILES
Temporary logs are created as muffle-XXXXXX under TMPDIR (or /tmp). A
successful temporary log is removed. A failed temporary log is retained.
Persistent --log files remain after success and failure.
.SH SIGNALS
SIGINT and SIGTERM are forwarded to the child process group. If the child
remains alive after the grace interval, Muffle sends SIGKILL. Descendants that
leave the process group may not be terminated.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Child stdout and stderr are combined. Muffle does not allocate a pseudo-
terminal, preserve interactive terminal behavior, or support native Windows.
Logs are not redacted or encrypted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
muffle -- cmake --build build
muffle --tail 10 -- make test
muffle --verbose -- cargo test
muffle --log build.log -- npm test
muffle -- sh -c 'make && make test'
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sh (1),
.I https://github.com/Thavarshan/muffle
